WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.555 --> 00:00:08.265
Hi!

00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:09.187
I'm Ana.

00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:10.799
Welcome to 'What to Say'!

00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:35.572
Do you know what to say when you discuss advantages and disadvantages?

00:00:35.643 --> 00:00:41.330
Listen out for useful language for discussing advantages and disadvantages.

00:00:41.494 --> 00:00:44.541
Then, we'll practise saying the new phrases –

00:00:44.822 --> 00:00:46.283
after this.

00:00:46.635 --> 00:00:49.543
So, table tennis,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.277
bean bags,

00:00:51.512 --> 00:00:53.043
 board games,

00:00:53.074 --> 00:00:54.769
video games!

00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:57.379
Hey, how about a trampoline?

00:00:57.574 --> 00:00:59.002
Stop right there.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.838
I love your ideas, Noelia, but a trampoline? Really?

00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:05.533
Absolutely.

00:01:06.174 --> 00:01:08.374
When do you have your best ideas?

00:01:09.104 --> 00:01:12.437
I don't know. Usually when I'm

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:14.567
 cooking, I suppose.

00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:15.708
Exactly.

00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:20.637
We often have our best ideas when we are away from our desks.

00:01:20.927 --> 00:01:25.765
The other day I was on a trampoline and the vision for the creativity room

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.757
came to me.

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:29.858
Why were you on a trampo…?

00:01:30.164 --> 00:01:31.077
Never mind.

00:01:31.336 --> 00:01:32.085
Look,

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:36.980
on the one hand it's a lovely idea and it fits with our brand,

00:01:37.215 --> 00:01:44.370
but on the other hand it could be noisy and chaotic and maybe too much fun!

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:45.292
But

00:01:45.332 --> 00:01:47.795
having fun helps you be creative,

00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:51.553
and being creative is vital to our business!

00:01:52.194 --> 00:01:57.467
I see what you mean, but I'm just not sure if a trampoline is necessary.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:04.006
 Also, there could be an issue with the clients arriving at the office and seeing us all jumping around.

00:02:04.428 --> 00:02:09.426
I see where you're coming from, but I think our clients will love it!

00:02:10.387 --> 00:02:15.933
And there are lots of advantages to trampolining. It's good for the body and the mind.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.887
Maybe, but I can also see the disadvantages.

00:02:20.957 --> 00:02:23.157
What if someone hurts themselves?

00:02:23.841 --> 00:02:25.729
But we're all adults.

00:02:26.643 --> 00:02:28.486
And we can get extra insurance.

00:02:28.526 --> 00:02:30.326
Come on! It's a great idea!

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.765
OK, I'll think about it.

00:02:34.906 --> 00:02:37.281
Perfect. I'll email you some links!

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:40.492
I haven't said yes!

00:02:42.039 --> 00:02:43.758
Oh, Noelia!

00:02:45.766 --> 00:02:46.766
Hello again!

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.843
A trampoline in the office?

00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:50.859
Well, there's an idea!

00:02:51.649 --> 00:02:58.188
 So, did you notice the useful phrases used for discussing advantages and disadvantages?

00:02:58.251 --> 00:03:00.446
 Listen to me and then repeat.

00:03:00.751 --> 00:03:03.727
On the one hand …, but on the other hand …

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:09.489
On the one hand …, but on the other hand …

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.317
I see what you mean, but I'm just not sure.

00:03:18.442 --> 00:03:21.309
I see what you mean, but I'm just not sure.

00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:26.574
There could be an issue with that.

00:03:29.184 --> 00:03:31.160
There could be an issue with that.

00:03:33.887 --> 00:03:37.669
I see where you're coming from, but I think they'll love it.

00:03:41.717 --> 00:03:45.037
I see where you're coming from, but I think they'll love it.

00:03:48.909 --> 00:03:50.842
There are lots of advantages.

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:55.913
There are lots of advantages.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.505
Maybe, but I can also see the disadvantages.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:10.310
Maybe, but I can also see the disadvantages.

00:04:13.865 --> 00:04:20.286
Try and use some of these phrases the next time you discuss advantages and disadvantages in English.

00:04:20.802 --> 00:04:22.294
Bye for now!

